WEBVTT

1
00:00:17.035 --> 00:00:17.655
said Dad.

2
00:00:18.195 --> 00:00:19.736
Joy reached into her sack.

3
00:00:19.756 --> 00:00:23.417
"Nail!" she said, handing him one.

4
00:00:23.997 --> 00:00:26.779
Dad pounded it into a board with his hammer.

5
00:00:26.799 --> 00:00:28.699
"Good job!"

6
00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:29.740
said Joy.

7
00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:33.681
Joy and her dad had been busy all morning.

8
00:00:34.802 --> 00:00:37.683
They had moved Grandpa's wood up to the elm trees.

9
00:00:39.464 --> 00:00:42.925
Then they bought more wooden boards and posts at the lumberyard.

10
00:00:44.106 --> 00:00:48.468
Dad put two posts in the ground and built a frame for the tree house floor.

11
00:00:49.588 --> 00:00:52.769
When he was finished, he looked at Joy with a frown.

12
00:00:52.789 --> 00:00:56.691
"Partner," he said, "we have a problem."

13
00:00:56.711 --> 00:00:58.792
"What's wrong?"

14
00:00:59.356 --> 00:01:00.797
asked Joy with surprise.

15
00:01:00.817 --> 00:01:03.658
"See this wood we bought for the floor?"

16
00:01:04.258 --> 00:01:07.119
said Dad, pointing at a pile of 12 boards.

17
00:01:07.139 --> 00:01:09.961
"They are two and a half meters long."

18
00:01:11.081 --> 00:01:14.823
Joy looked at the boards and then looked up at the frame Dad had built.

19
00:01:16.023 --> 00:01:18.184
She tilted her head and narrowed her eyes.

20
00:01:19.905 --> 00:01:21.045
Then she smiled.

21
00:01:21.605 --> 00:01:23.646
"Those boards look too long."

22
00:01:24.807 --> 00:01:26.387
"You've got a good set of eyes!"

23
00:01:26.868 --> 00:01:27.488
said Dad.

24
00:01:28.556 --> 00:01:33.139
"The frame is two meters long, so we need to shorten each board by half a meter."

25
00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:36.622
Dad and Joy knelt by one board.

26
00:01:36.642 --> 00:01:42.386
"Hold this tape measure at the end of the board," Dad said, handing her the measure.

27
00:01:43.526 --> 00:01:45.528
Then he pulled the tape along the edge.

28
00:01:45.548 --> 00:01:49.851
"That's 25 centimeters," said Joy.

29
00:01:50.431 --> 00:01:52.012
Dad pulled the tape some more.

30
00:01:52.032 --> 00:01:54.254
"And that's 50!"

31
00:01:54.274 --> 00:01:59.938
"Now I mark it with a pencil," explained Dad as he drew a black line.

32
00:01:59.958 --> 00:02:02.439
"That's where we will cut the board."

33
00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:05.402
"Should we measure and mark all of them?"

34
00:02:05.942 --> 00:02:06.542
asked Joy.

35
00:02:06.562 --> 00:02:09.024
"Yes," said Dad.

36
00:02:09.044 --> 00:02:11.606
"Then I'll cut them down to the right size.

37
00:02:12.767 --> 00:02:13.427
And you know what?

38
00:02:13.928 --> 00:02:16.209
We can take the leftover wood to the recycling center."

39
00:02:16.229 --> 00:02:20.772
"Somebody else will be able to use it," said Joy.

40
00:02:20.792 --> 00:02:23.374
"Just like we used Grandpa's wood."

41
00:02:24.635 --> 00:02:29.189
By late afternoon Dad had finished nailing the tree house floor to the frame.

42
00:02:30.429 --> 00:02:34.771
He and Joy sat on the back end of the truck and looked up at their work.

43
00:02:34.791 --> 00:02:36.951
"What's next?"

44
00:02:37.491 --> 00:02:38.112
asked Joy.

45
00:02:38.132 --> 00:02:40.652
"Let's recycle that extra wood.

46
00:02:41.092 --> 00:02:44.173
We might find a few things we need too," said Dad.

47
00:02:45.334 --> 00:02:48.435
They got in the truck and drove down the hill to the road.

48
00:02:49.975 --> 00:02:53.116
When they reached the center, Joy hopped out of the truck.

49
00:02:54.348 --> 00:02:59.151
She liked looking up at the mountains of crushed cardboard and smashed soda cans.

50
00:03:00.152 --> 00:03:00.892
She saw Mr.

51
00:03:00.932 --> 00:03:02.793
Ramirez, Carlos' father.

52
00:03:03.954 --> 00:03:09.657
He was in charge of sorting all the metal—brass, tin, iron, steel, and copper.

53
00:03:09.677 --> 00:03:11.578
"Hello, Mr.

54
00:03:11.618 --> 00:03:13.399
Ramirez," called Joy.

55
00:03:13.419 --> 00:03:16.300
"Dad and I are building a tree house!

56
00:03:16.901 --> 00:03:18.441
Do you have anything we can use?"

57
00:03:18.461 --> 00:03:21.923
"Well, let's see," said Mr.

58
00:03:21.983 --> 00:03:23.945
Ramirez. "Do you need a bucket?"

59
00:03:23.965 --> 00:03:27.047
"We might," replied Joy.

60
00:03:27.067 --> 00:03:31.670
"Thanks!" Dad was looking in a cardboard box.

61
00:03:32.311 --> 00:03:34.432
"Here are some old hooks," he said.

62
00:03:34.452 --> 00:03:38.395
"The kids can hang stuff on those," said Mr.

63
00:03:38.415 --> 00:03:42.338
Ramirez. Joy dropped the hooks into her bucket.

64
00:03:42.358 --> 00:03:44.479
"What's this?"

65
00:03:45.119 --> 00:03:45.780
asked Joy.

66
00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:46.941
"A wheel?"

67
00:03:46.961 --> 00:03:50.723
"It's a special kind of wheel," said Mr.

68
00:03:50.763 --> 00:03:53.505
Ramirez. "It's called a pulley.

69
00:03:54.026 --> 00:03:56.348
You use it with a rope to help lift something."

70
00:03:57.489 --> 00:03:58.810
Joy turned to her dad.

71
00:03:58.830 --> 00:04:00.211
"Do we need one?"

72
00:04:00.231 --> 00:04:02.773
"Take it," he said.

73
00:04:02.793 --> 00:04:04.114
"We can use it."

74
00:04:04.134 --> 00:04:09.039
"Let's take this pole too," said Joy.

75
00:04:09.059 --> 00:04:10.960
"It might be good for something."

76
00:04:12.141 --> 00:04:15.504
Then Dad found some sheets of tin leaning against a wall.

77
00:04:15.524 --> 00:04:18.067
"Our tree house roof!"

78
00:04:18.627 --> 00:04:19.388
cried Joy.

79
00:04:20.829 --> 00:04:21.910
And that wasn't all.

80
00:04:22.371 --> 00:04:25.896
They also found a small window frame and an old door.

81
00:04:27.038 --> 00:04:30.504
They piled everything in the back of the truck and drove home.
